<p>
  <strong>Onitsuka Tiger</strong> is ASICS' lifestyle line, founded in 1949 in Kobe, Japan by Kihachiro Onitsuka. The brand pioneered the modern running sneaker (the 1950s Marathon Tabi) and today shapes the runways of Mihara Yasuhiro, Andrea Pompilio and streets across major cities worldwide.
</p>
<p>
  At Resell Lausanne, we offer an authentic <strong>Onitsuka Tiger</strong> selection for Switzerland: Mexico 66, Tokuten, Serrano, GSM, Delegation, California 78, Mexico 66 SD and collaborations with Naked Copenhagen, Mihara Yasuhiro and Cecilie Bahnsen. Every pair is authenticated by our team. Free delivery in Switzerland from CHF 50 (CHF 10 in Europe).
</p>

<h3>Onitsuka Tiger Mexico 66 — The signature silhouette</h3>
<p>
  Launched in 1966 for the Mexico Olympics, the Mexico 66 became globally famous through Uma Thurman in Kill Bill (yellow and black) and a fashion comeback in the 2010s. Nappa leather, slim EVA sole, contrasting ASICS stripes. Colourways include Birch/Green, White/Red, Black/White, Cream/Peacoat, Pink Salt and many limited editions.
</p>

<h3>Onitsuka Tiger Tokuten — Running heritage revisited</h3>
<p>
  The Tokuten revives codes from 1980s Onitsuka marathon shoes: breathable mesh, low-cut upper, integrated gel and dual-density sole. A runway favourite for Cecilie Bahnsen and widely worn across the new Korean and Japanese fashion wave.
</p>

<h3>Onitsuka Tiger Mexico 66 SD and collaborations</h3>
<p>
  The SD (Super Deluxe) range uses premium materials: nubuck leather, Japanese suede and leather lining. Naked Copenhagen, Mihara Yasuhiro, Sanrio (Hello Kitty) and Andrea Pompilio collaborations release in limited quantities and remain highly sought after on the secondary market.
</p>

<h3>How to spot authentic Onitsuka Tiger sneakers</h3>
<p>
  Check leather grain, ASICS stripe consistency, the inner label showing country of manufacture (Vietnam, Indonesia or Japan for SD models), the Onitsuka Tiger stamp on the insole and stitching quality. Our team verifies every pair before shipping and includes a certificate of authenticity.
</p>

